&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trumid is a dynamic fintech revolutionizing the landscape of fixed income trading. With intelligent, easy-to-use, electronic solutions, we are rapidly growing and seeking exceptional talent to help redefine the boundaries of technology and finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2014 by a team of fixed income market experts, Trumid has quickly become one of the top three corporate bond e-trading platforms in the U.S. Today, over 1,300 traders from an extensive and expanding client network of 890+ buy-and sell-side institutions transact on Trumid monthly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a rich history of innovation and a unique ability to innovate at scale, we collaborate closely with our clients, iterating quickly toward optimal solutions. With market share and client engagement at all-time highs and our pace of product development faster than ever, this is an exciting and transformative time at Trumid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our business model thrives on participation, and so does our company culture. We rely on every team member’s contribution to help us accomplish our goals. To succeed at Trumid, you must be curious, passionate about your craft, ambitious, collaborative, and driven.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Emerging Markets (EM) Sales team, you will work within an experienced and expert team growing the demand for our electronic trading platform. You will be responsible for buyside and sellside client relationship management, including identification of new prospect accounts, on-boarding and managing on-going relationships. You will speak to EM clients, creating awareness around liquidity and trading activity. You will be responsible for demoing the platform and assisting clients execute trades on the platform. A successful candidate will have the ability to develop, grow and maintain relationships. You should have strong communication skills to teach clients how to use the technology and demonstrate the benefits to their workflow. You should be a proactive self-starter, hardworking and possess strong critical thinking skills to enhance participation on the platform and increase revenue.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our New York City office and operates under a hybrid work model. Given the highly collaborative nature of the Emerging Markets Sales team, team members are expected to be in the office four (4) days per week, with the flexibility to work remotely up to one (1) day per week, subject to business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you do?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become highly attuned to the pulse of the market: key geopolitical and company news and events; buyer vs seller imbalances; general trends in credit and fixed income markets overall.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be resourceful, using market intelligence to identify opportunities to help our clients address their risk needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently and energetically engage with traders to determine their priorities weekly, daily and intraday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of how to gauge supply and demand for EM sovereign and corporate credits in real time, including how to estimate moves at the market open and sensitivity to certain macro events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn and master the Trumid product offering so you can direct traders to the optimal workflow for their respective trading priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain and deepen relationships with traders via desk visits, social outings and group events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage your curiosity and relationships to help make the Trumid platform better: solicit feedback and generate ideas for new and innovative workflow solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate enthusiasm for problem-solving and workflow solutions.&amp;nbsp; Demonstrate openness and capacity to learn and apply AI to streamline Trumid&#39;s daily processes as well as those of our clients.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Economics, Business Administration, or a related field preferred; however, candidates from all academic backgrounds with a strong interest in financial markets are encouraged to apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-5 years’ experience in markets facing role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Series 7 and Series 63&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for markets, trading, credit and FinTech with desire to expand knowledge of fixed income products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and decision making; curiosity and willingness to learn how the business functions strategically&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional interpersonal skills; relentlessness, incredible follow-up skills and ability to navigate and operate in a fast-paced environment - must be a proactive, self-starter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team – someone who is collaborative, committed, flexible and reliable with a strong &quot;can do” attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel domestically for in-person client meetings and events; and be available to join and host after-working-hours client entertainment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI tools and a curiosity for how emerging technologies can enhance workflows, automate repetitive tasks, and drive smarter decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid medical, dental and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily in-office lunch stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-oriented and collaborative company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lively and dynamic office space with fully stocked kitchen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In compliance with New York City Pay Transparency Law, the base salary range for this role in New York City is between $95,000 - $150,000. This range does not include discretionary bonus or other forms of compensation or benefits offered in connection with this job. Several factors are considered when determining a candidate’s compensation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trumid is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note: All communication from Trumid’s recruiting team comes from @trumid.com email addresses. We conduct remote interviews via Zoom only. We will never ask you to purchase equipment, download software (other than Zoom), or share sensitive personal information during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trumid is a dynamic fintech revolutionizing the landscape of fixed income trading. With intelligent, easy-to-use, electronic solutions, we are rapidly growing and seeking exceptional talent to help redefine the boundaries of technology and finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2014 by a team of fixed income market experts, Trumid has quickly become one of the top three corporate bond e-trading platforms in the U.S. Today, over 1,300 traders from an extensive and expanding client network of 890+ buy-and sell-side institutions transact on Trumid monthly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a rich history of innovation and a unique ability to innovate at scale, we collaborate closely with our clients, iterating quickly toward optimal solutions. With market share and client engagement at all-time highs and our pace of product development faster than ever, this is an exciting and transformative time at Trumid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our business model thrives on participation, and so does our company culture. We rely on every team member&#39;s contribution to help us accomplish our goals. To succeed at Trumid, you must be curious, passionate about your craft, ambitious, collaborative, and driven.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Integration Product owns how customers and strategic partners connect to our platform — the data feeds, order flows, and trade messaging that link external systems to ours. We build and maintain that connectivity directly, and we partner with every trading protocol team on the integration side of their work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role&#39;s mandate is simple: &lt;strong&gt;keep teams aligned, unblocked, and moving.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In practice, that means fielding the steady stream of inbound from across the org, representing Integration Product in the internal meetings and conversations where we need a seat at the table, and partnering with the Product Owner on the spec and decision work that keeps delivery moving. You&#39;ll be the first-line filter for internal stakeholder questions, the person who knows where product initiatives stand across our workstreams, and help make sure nothing falls between the cracks when feature delivery work touches multiple teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Documentation and Jira hygiene are part of the role, but AI handles a growing share of that work. The real value of this hire is in communication, coordination, judgment, and the ability to walk into an ambiguous situation and walk out with a plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Head of Integration Product and is aligned with U.S. trading hours, with typical business hours of 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM ET. The position is based in our New York City office and follows a hybrid work schedule, with employees expected to work onsite several days per week to support collaboration with clients, trading partners, and cross-functional teams across Sales, Product, and Technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run interference.&lt;/strong&gt; Field questions from product, dev, and QA across all of the organization&#39;s delivery teams. Translate product intent, clarify requirements, support bug triage, and resolve in-flight spec questions. Answer what you can, route what you can&#39;t, escalate when judgment is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent Integration Product in cross-team forums&lt;/strong&gt;. Sit in team standups, design reviews, initiative huddles, and rollout planning sessions. Take the action items, follow up, and make sure commitments get tracked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner on specs across pipelines.&lt;/strong&gt; Help outline and maintain specs for the Integration pipeline, and review planned features from other pipelines for integration dependencies and downstream impact. Collaborate with protocol teams to scope, document, and validate integration-affecting features even when another team leads development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Surface and unblock dependencies.&lt;/strong&gt; Track what&#39;s in flight, spot potential blockers early, and chase down the answers needed to keep work moving. Notice when something has gone quiet and ping the right people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make tactical product decisions.&lt;/strong&gt; Operate within the Product Owner&#39;s strategic framework to refine acceptance criteria, prioritize enhancements, and validate delivery scope — escalating when a call goes beyond the framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute grounded roadmap input.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring delivery velocity, developer feedback, and operational pain points back into roadmap conversations. Identify tactical improvements that compound team efficiency over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain documentation and ticket workflows.&lt;/strong&gt; Draft and maintain Confluence pages, keep Jira tickets clean, help structure specs. AI handles more of the drafting every quarter — your job is to make sure the output is right and the workflow holds together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate release and rollout.&lt;/strong&gt; Run internal release readiness: coordinate dependencies, internal documentation, and cross-team communication for go-lives. Support the Product Owner on GTM for FIX-affecting changes, including release sequencing and enablement work alongside Integration Success. Ensure that all GTM materials (external FIX specs, conformance tests guides, and release notes) are ready to be used and help coordinate internal training sessions for new features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reduce the load over time.&lt;/strong&gt; Spot patterns in what&#39;s eating the team&#39;s time and propose ways to reduce it — better docs, clearer processes, lightweight tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect to teach the domain, these are the key skills that will make this role succeed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Up to 4 years of experience;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong self-motivator.&lt;/strong&gt; You see what needs doing and do it, and you know when to ask before acting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem solver.&lt;/strong&gt; You can walk into ambiguity, ask the right questions, and come out with a clear game plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent at aligning teams.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re comfortable in cross-functional rooms, you read what people actually need vs. what they&#39;re asking for, and you&#39;re good at getting groups to a shared answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sharp written and verbal communicator.&lt;/strong&gt; You know the difference between a summary, an ask, and a status update (and which one is needed when).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable with shifting priorities.&lt;/strong&gt; Our work touches every team, which means our day rarely looks like our plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious and ramps fast.&lt;/strong&gt; You pick up new domains quickly and aren&#39;t intimidated by depth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with FIX protocol or other electronic trading protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed income or institutional trading background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Jira, Confluence, Slack, and modern PM tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior product, project management, business analyst, or development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid medical, dental and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-oriented and collaborative company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility for in-office and work from home arrangements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In compliance with New York City Pay Transparency Law, the base salary range for this role in New York City is between &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;$95,000 – $130,000.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; This range does not include discretionary bonus or other forms of compensation or benefits offered in connection with this job. Several factors are considered when determining a candidate’s compensation. Please note that the salary range listed for this position is based on the level of experience outlined in the job description. If a candidate’s experience differs from the requirements, the salary may be adjusted accordingly.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trumid is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note: All communication from Trumid’s recruiting team comes from @trumid.com email addresses. We conduct remote interviews via Zoom only. We will never ask you to purchase equipment, download software (other than Zoom), or share sensitive personal information during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trumid is a dynamic fintech revolutionizing the landscape of fixed income trading. With intelligent, easy-to-use, electronic solutions, we are rapidly growing and seeking exceptional talent to help redefine the boundaries of technology and finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2014 by a team of fixed income market experts, Trumid has quickly become one of the top three corporate bond e-trading platforms in the U.S. Today, over 1,300 traders from an extensive and expanding client network of 890+ buy-and sell-side institutions transact on Trumid monthly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a rich history of innovation and a unique ability to innovate at scale, we collaborate closely with our clients, iterating quickly toward optimal solutions. With market share and client engagement at all-time highs and our pace of product development faster than ever, this is an exciting and transformative time at Trumid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our business model thrives on participation, and so does our company culture. We rely on every team member’s contribution to help us accomplish our goals. To succeed at Trumid, you must be curious, passionate about your craft, ambitious, collaborative, and driven.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trumid is seeking a Senior Data Engineer to join our Data &amp;amp; Intelligence team and build the analytics platform that powers reporting, decision-making, and data delivery across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will use dbt to design and implement scalable data models in BigQuery aimed at making&amp;nbsp; complex data digestible for internal and external stakeholders via reports and BI tools as well as agentic AI products within our tech stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role focuses primarily on building the data models and datasets that power analytics and reporting, rather than working exclusively on dashboards. As part of the broader data platform team, engineers may occasionally contribute to reporting or visualization work when needed to support stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also help establish best practices for data governance, documentation, testing, and metric definition across the analytics platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is U.S.-based, with remote or hybrid options available. Candidates located in New York City are preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Tech Stack.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BigQuery, dbt, Fivetran, SQL-based data modeling, and modern analytics and semantic layer tools. We rely heavily on AI-powered IDEs and agentic workflows for development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Build.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curated data models in BigQuery using dbt that define consistent business metrics across Trumid&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data delivery systems that support dashboards, client-facing reporting, compliance datasets, and other external data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Governed datasets and documentation that enable self-service analytics across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement scalable data models in BigQuery using dbt that power analytics, reporting, and operational insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop systems for delivering data to internal stakeholders and external clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain data governance practices including documentation, lineage, testing, and data quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize query performance and cost efficiency for analytics workloads in BigQuery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, sales, analytics, and executive stakeholders to translate business requirements into reliable data models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and analysts on analytics engineering and data modeling best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the broader data platform, collaborating with engineers building real-time data systems and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building analytics or data platform infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in SQL and dbt, including complex transformation logic and data modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing data warehouse models in BigQuery or similar cloud data warehouses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data modeling patterns in columnar databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building curated datasets used by analysts and business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with modern data stack tools such as Fivetran or similar ingestion frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to collaborate with non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring for multiple roles and levels on this team. Candidates whose experience aligns more closely with another level may be considered for that role during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid medical, dental and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-oriented and collaborative company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In compliance with New York City Pay Transparency Law, the base salary range for this role in New York City is between $200,000- $250,000. This range does not include discretionary bonus or other forms of compensation or benefits offered in connection with this job. Several factors are considered when determining a candidate’s compensation. Please note that the salary range listed for this position is based on the level of experience outlined in the job description. If a candidate&#39;s experience differs from the requirements, the salary may be adjusted accordingly.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trumid is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note: All communication from Trumid&#39;s recruiting team comes from @trumid.com email addresses. We conduct remote interviews via Zoom only. We will never ask you to purchase equipment, download software (other than Zoom), or share sensitive personal information during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trumid is a dynamic fintech revolutionizing the landscape of fixed income trading. With intelligent, easy-to-use, electronic solutions, we are rapidly growing and seeking exceptional talent to help redefine the boundaries of technology and finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2014 by a team of fixed income market experts, Trumid has quickly become one of the top three corporate bond e-trading platforms in the U.S. Today, over 1,300 traders from an extensive and expanding client network of 1,000+ buy- and sell-side institutions transact on Trumid monthly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a rich history of innovation and a unique ability to innovate at scale, we collaborate closely with our clients, iterating quickly toward optimal solutions. With market share and client engagement at all-time highs and our pace of product development faster than ever, this is an exciting and transformative time at Trumid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our business model thrives on participation, and so does our company culture. We rely on every team member&#39;s contribution to help us accomplish our goals. To succeed at Trumid, you must be curious, passionate about your craft, ambitious, collaborative, and driven. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.trumid.com/&quot;&gt;www.trumid.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team as a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, building the trading systems at the core of our platform. We have recently been migrating critical trading workflows onto Aeron-based sequenced-log architecture and this role sits at the heart of that platform: you will join one of the teams running services on top of it, matched to the team that best fits your strengths and interests during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are also an AI-native engineering organization: the majority of our pull requests are AI-written and AI-reviewed, supported by in-house agent tooling built directly into our monorepo, so engineers spend their time on design, correctness, and leverage rather than boilerplate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an engineer with a background in capital markets, trading workflows, or electronic trading systems. You have strong skills in system design, you focus on observability and testing, and you leverage AI to move faster without sacrificing quality. Within your first six months, you will tackle key projects such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feature Expansion: &lt;/strong&gt;Ship new trading protocol capabilities at high velocity on our Aeron-based platform, supporting a growing client base and increased trading volumes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Modernization: &lt;/strong&gt;Evolve our service architecture — migrating remaining workflows onto the new stack and designing the messaging patterns that connect it to the rest of the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Optimization: &lt;/strong&gt;Improve platform scalability, performance, and test coverage for systems where correctness is the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design, Develop and Test:&lt;/strong&gt; Build protocols and features to meet functional and non-functional requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support and Maintain:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure the reliability and availability of services developed by the team, addressing production issues and continuously improving operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Improve system performance for low latency and high throughput, crucial in trading systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with cross-functional teams to execute projects and contribute to a team-oriented culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking an engineer with experience in financial services, trade workflows, or electronic trading systems. Your qualifications include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;U.S., EST Time Zone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years of experience in software engineering, preferably in capital markets or trading workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in JVM-based languages (Scala preferred); ability to write clean and maintainable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience in designing, implementing, and maintaining scalable systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network Protocols &amp;amp; Messaging:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with technologies such as TCP/IP, FIX, Kafka, or Aeron.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Technologies:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with Kubernetes and Docker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Assisted Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to effectively use AI-assisted development tools (e.g. Claude Code) to accelerate delivery and improve quality while maintaining strong engineering judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of low latency, high-throughput systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SDLC Practices:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) methodologies, including agile practices and CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Commitment to delivering high-quality solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More About Us and our Tech Stack.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages and Frameworks&lt;/strong&gt;: We primarily use Scala with ZIO, Pekko and gRPC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Messaging Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;: Our messaging systems include Kafka and Aeron.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Containerization and Orchestration&lt;/strong&gt;: We rely on Kubernetes and Docker to build, deliver, and scale containerized services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Native Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Agent tooling, automated review, and AI-assisted workflows are built into our development platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Culture&lt;/strong&gt;: We value a collaborative team environment where your technical views and leadership abilities are highly appreciated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
